# Backend env (Python)
#
# Set these on the host (Railway, Fly, Render, your own VPS, etc.):
#
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS — comma-separated list of FE origins permitted to call this
#                    backend via CORS. The dev defaults (localhost:5173, etc.)
#                    are baked in; in production you MUST set this to your
#                    actual FE origin(s), e.g.:
#                      ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://app.your-domain.com,https://staging.your-domain.com
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY        — required for LLM turns (real-time or chat). SYSTEM DEFAULT
#                        — the FE can override per-user via Settings → API.
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY      — optional; STT/TTS provider. SYSTEM DEFAULT.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY    — optional; TTS provider. SYSTEM DEFAULT.
# TWILIO_*              — required for live call routing (account_sid, auth_token, phone_number)
# PUBLIC_URL            — public HTTPS URL the backend is reachable from (Twilio webhook target)
# PORT                  — defaults to 8080
#
# CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY — Fernet key for encrypting per-user provider
#                              credentials at rest. The FE never sees the
#                              plaintext on disk; only the BE can decrypt.
#                              Generate with:
#                                python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
#                              The value must be exactly those 44 characters.
#                              A placeholder (e.g. "your_fernet_key_here"), a
#                              hex digest, or a truncated key is REJECTED at
#                              startup with the reason.
#                              REQUIRED in production: with no key the app
#                              refuses to start (encrypted credentials would
#                              be unreadable after a restart). It is only
#                              optional in dev, where ENVIRONMENT is one of
#                              development/dev/local/test and an ephemeral
#                              key is generated instead — set it anyway so
#                              saved credentials survive a restart.
#                              Rotating it: keep the old value in
#                              CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_PREVIOUS_KEYS so the
#                              rows encrypted with it stay readable.
#
# Auth bootstrap (only required for the FIRST admin):
#   python scripts/seed_admin.py
# Sets the admin email to admin@revolutionmedia.ai with the password
# Adminrevolutionmedia@109 (see the script to change it before running).

# Microsoft Dynamics 365 / Dataverse OAuth (multi-tenant Entra application)
# DYNAMICS365_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# DYNAMICS365_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-entra-client-secret
# DYNAMICS365_REDIRECT_URI=https://your-backend.example/integrations/dynamics365/oauth/callback
# Optional override; the default requests offline access and Global Discovery.
# DYNAMICS365_SCOPES=openid profile email offline_access https://globaldisco.crm.dynamics.com/.default
